# (0.24) The screen saver (DESK=1; tests/mousegen.py makes tests/saver.keys from this; the
# card's /SYSTEM/CONFIG says saver=4: it starts after 4 s without input, the test hook).
# Small pointer moves keep it away until 9 s. Shots (s):
#   1  10.5  the desktop with Files (the picture to come back to)
#   2  15.0  the saver (started at about 13 s): the sprites on black (REV $0B), or the
#            stripes block alone, drawn by the CPU (REV $0A and older: no sprites)
#   3  17.5  a key (16 s) woke it: the desktop exactly as in shot 1
#   4  19.0  the pointer on the SD card icon (not clicked)
#   5  24.0  the saver again
#   6  26.5  a click (25 s) woke it and was swallowed: the desktop exactly as in shot 4 (the
#            SD card icon not selected)
#   7  30.0  Settings: the "Screen saver" row (Off, 1 min, 5 min, 10 min, Test; 4 s is none of
#            them)
#   8  32.5  Test clicked (31 s): the saver at once
#   9  35.0  a key (33.5 s) woke it: Settings as in shot 7, with the pointer on Test
#  10  48.0  BASIC (Programs > BASIC) runs a full-screen program (SCREEN 1: GCLS 20, a VSYNC loop) since
#            about 42 s: no saver while a program holds the full screen
#  11  51.5  Esc (49 s): Break, the BASIC window back
#  12  58.0  F12 (52 s): the classic Atari (black in emu816), no saver while it is shown
#  13  60.0  F12 again (58.5 s): the desktop as it was (BASIC's window)
1500 move 321 180
3000 move 320 180
4500 move 321 180
6000 move 320 180
7500 move 321 180
9000 move 320 180
16000 key a
18000 move 595 45
25000 click
27000 move 40 8
27400 click
27900 move 40 38
28300 click
30500 move 465 290
31000 click
33500 key a
35500 key {esc}
36500 move 100 8
36900 click
37400 move 100 52
37800 click
40000 key 10 SCREEN 1:GCLS 20\n20 VSYNC:GOTO 20\nRUN\n
49000 key {esc}
52000 key {F12}
58500 key {F12}
